# Dragon Magazine Compendium - Mariner (reprint), loaded only without Legends of the Twins.

###Block: Mariner Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Mariner ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Cutlass|Net|Scimitar|Trident	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight	AUTO:SHIELDPROF|SHIELDTYPE=Buckler	SOURCEPAGE:p.337	DESC:A mariner is proficient with all simple weapons, plus the cutlass, net, scimitar, and trident. A mariner is proficient with light armor and buckler shields.
Bonus Feat	KEY:Mariner ~ Bonus Feat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:Pool_MarinerFeat|0	BONUS:VAR|Pool_MarinerFeat|1+floor(MarinerLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.337	DESC:At 1st, 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th level a mariner gains a bonus feat from the mariner bonus feat list (%1 so far). He must still meet all prerequisites for a bonus feat, including ability score and base attack bonus minimums.|Pool_MarinerFeat
Sailor Lore	KEY:Mariner ~ Sailor Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MarinerSailorLore|0	BONUS:VAR|MarinerSailorLore|MarinerLVL+INT	SOURCEPAGE:p.338	DESC:A mariner may make a special sailor lore check with a bonus equal to his mariner level + his Intelligence modifier (+%1) to see whether he knows relevant information about local people or history, far away places, or strange superstitions. The information isn't necessarily true. He may not take 10 or 20 on this check. DC 10 commonly known, 20 known by select groups, 25 known only by few individuals, 30 unknown to the vast majority.|MarinerSailorLore
Seamanship	KEY:Mariner ~ Seamanship	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MarinerSeamanship|0	BONUS:VAR|MarinerSeamanship|floor((MarinerLVL+3)/4)	BONUS:SKILL|Balance,Climb,Profession (Sailor)|MarinerSeamanship|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.338	DESC:A mariner gains a +%1 competence bonus on all Balance, Climb, and Profession (sailor) checks (+1 at 1st level, +2 at 5th, +3 at 9th, +4 at 13th, +5 at 17th).|MarinerSeamanship
Dirty Strike	KEY:Mariner ~ Dirty Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MarinerDirtyStrike|0	BONUS:VAR|MarinerDirtyStrike|floor((MarinerLVL+2)/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.338	DESC:As a full-round action, a mariner may make a single melee attack that deals an additional +%1d4 points of damage of the same kind as the weapon's damage (nonlethal if the attack deals nonlethal damage). It has no effect on creatures without a discernible anatomy or immune to critical hits, such as constructs, oozes, plants, or undead, and is not multiplied on a critical hit (+1d4 at 2nd level, +2d4 at 6th, +3d4 at 10th, +4d4 at 14th, +5d4 at 18th).|MarinerDirtyStrike
Back-to-Back	KEY:Mariner ~ Back-to-Back	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Mariner Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MarinerBackToBack|0	BONUS:VAR|MarinerBackToBack|floor(MarinerLVL/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.338	DESC:Whenever a mariner is adjacent to an ally and fighting defensively, using total defense or the Combat Expertise feat, he gains a +%1 dodge bonus to his AC (+1 at 4th level, +2 at 8th, +3 at 12th, +4 at 16th, +5 at 20th). He loses this bonus if he is denied his Dexterity bonus to AC or if he or his ally moves more than 5 ft. away.|MarinerBackToBack
